<h2>Tips for Better Agents</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Use plain-language names</strong> – Name agents clearly, like "Send Renewal Reminder" instead of internal abbreviations or codes</li>
    <li><strong>Write helpful descriptions</strong> – Include a short, friendly description explaining when to use the agent</li>
    <li><strong>Choose appropriate icons</strong> – Select icons that visually match the task (envelope for emails, link for payment links, document for forms)</li>
    <li><strong>Start simple</strong> – Begin with basic agents that do one thing well, then add complexity as needed</li>
    <li><strong>Test before sharing</strong> – Always test your agent before making it available to your team</li>
    <li><strong>Iterate and improve</strong> – As you use agents, refine them based on what works and what doesn't</li>
    <li><strong>Organize with categories</strong> – Use categories to group related agents together</li>
</ul>

