<h2>Best Practices</h2>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Name clearly</strong> – Use descriptive names that anyone on your team can understand</li>
    <li><strong>Test thoroughly</strong> – Always test agents before making them available to others</li>
    <li><strong>Document purpose</strong> – Use descriptions to explain when and why to use each agent</li>
    <li><strong>Start simple</strong> – Build basic agents first, then add complexity as needed</li>
    <li><strong>Get feedback</strong> – Ask your team for input on agent names, descriptions, and functionality</li>
    <li><strong>Keep organized</strong> – Use categories to group related agents</li>
    <li><strong>Update regularly</strong> – Refine agents based on how they're actually being used</li>
</ul>

